# Ownership in this repo does double duty.
#
# The default owner is the team that owns the monitors this repo demonstrates.
# That is the only entry here meant to be a real reviewer.
#
# Everything else is deliberately fictional. The uploader parses this file to
# attribute test failures to code owners, and a demo where every failing test
# has the same owner demonstrates nothing — so each `app/` scenario is owned by
# an invented company team, giving failure attribution in the product something
# to show. Those handles do not resolve on GitHub. That is expected: GitHub
# flags them as unknown owners and never requests review from them.

* @trunk-io/flaky-tests

# Fictional owners, one invented company team per app/ scenario.
#
# These give failure attribution in the product something to show: a page of
# failures all owned by one team demonstrates nothing about owner attribution.
# None of these handles resolve, which is expected — GitHub flags them as unknown
# owners and never requests review from them.
#
# The paths are matched against each test's `file` attribute, which is why the
# vitest configs are rooted at the repository rather than at the package.
